WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

NOTE
APBv2.mp4 narration. Transcribed locally with whisper.cpp (base.en) and
corrected against focused re-transcriptions of each unclear segment.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.720
AI agents are gaining payment authority.

2
00:00:02.986 --> 00:00:05.972
APB makes the controls scale with them.
Let's test

3
00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:08.959
an €8,000 supplier payment.
The agent

4
00:00:08.959 --> 00:00:11.946
can prepare payments, but it does not
have authority to execute

5
00:00:11.946 --> 00:00:16.932
this one. Hidden text in the invoice attempts
to replace the approved beneficiary account.

6
00:00:16.932 --> 00:00:20.906
APB checks identity, delegated authority,
instruction integrity,

7
00:00:20.906 --> 00:00:23.892
beneficiary state and approval
before evaluating any payment route.

8
00:00:23.892 --> 00:00:26.879
The controls fail. APB returns

9
00:00:26.879 --> 00:00:29.866
STOP. No payment executes
and PayPal is

10
00:00:29.866 --> 00:00:35.732
not called. The Decision Receipt records
exactly what failed, under which policy, and why.

11
00:00:35.732 --> 00:00:38.799
Now add the missing controls.
The beneficiary is verified,

12
00:00:38.826 --> 00:00:43.412
approval is captured, and transaction-bound
execution authority is granted.

13
00:00:43.412 --> 00:00:47.786
Only now does APB compare eligible routes
and recheck the payment before execution.

14
00:00:47.786 --> 00:00:52.772
In this case PayPal wins.
Change the mandate, and another provider wins.

15
00:00:53.759 --> 00:00:56.746
APB remains neutral.
This is defensive co-scaling.

16
00:00:56.746 --> 00:01:02.719
Greater agent authority requires stronger
identity, policy, monitoring and evidence.

17
00:01:02.719 --> 00:01:05.706
APB World tests agents repeatedly.

18
00:01:05.706 --> 00:01:11.679
Critical security failures are gates,
not hidden inside an average score.
Start with an authority assessment.

19
00:01:11.679 --> 00:01:17.652
Test the guardrails safely in a sandbox.
Validate performance against real decisions in shadow mode.

20
00:01:17.652 --> 00:01:20.639
Activate runtime enforcement only
when the evidence supports it.

21
00:01:20.639 --> 00:01:26.612
APB turns payment-agent risk into measurable guardrails,
controlled payment authority and auditable evidence.

22
00:01:26.612 --> 00:01:32.479
If your organization is deploying or accepting
payment agents, let's evaluate one workflow together.
